    ><div class="iG3p5BPTlNwyRLjvK-H1S6ReEvrq3zqW9b" data-instant-type="container" id="iG3p5BPTlNwyRLjvK-H1S6ReEvrq3zqW9b"
      ><div conditionals="" class="iJA7IQD1jUBvZijQS-H1S6ReEvrq3zqW9b" data-instant-type="container"
        ><div class="ibC1jrowmfKnY7p8H-H1S6ReEvrq3zqW9b" data-instant-type="container"
          ><div data-instant-type="text" class="instant-rich-text iUnEVUI1bH5p4Xss0-H1S6ReEvrq3zqW9b"><p>What to expect...</p></div
          ><div data-instant-type="text" class="instant-rich-text iifk3dsWBlIfd951f-H1S6ReEvrq3zqW9b"
            ><p><strong>Introduction</strong></p
            ><p></p><p><a target="" rel="noopener noreferrer" class="instant-editor__link" href="#iQCaCkgSQpP4yhk60">What are the UK car seat laws?</a></p
            ><p></p><p><a target="" rel="noopener noreferrer" class="instant-editor__link" href="#iUEVuzBSMA4vOrNLZ">What type of seat do I need?</a></p
            ><p></p><p><a target="" rel="noopener noreferrer" class="instant-editor__link" href="#itziZrCWlBfJdBQrs">What features should I look for?</a></p
            ><p></p><p><a target="" rel="noopener noreferrer" class="instant-editor__link" href="#i4ELJA0oJOCTvZFfg">Why should I rear face?</a></p
            ><p></p></div></div
        ><div class="iR7Orx8v2QLmYaJQT-H1S6ReEvrq3zqW9b" data-instant-type="container"
          ><div data-instant-type="text" class="instant-rich-text iPTd2pTZ4aKeILDAB-H1S6ReEvrq3zqW9b"
            ><p>As a first-time parent choosing a car seat can feel overwhelming to say the least.<em> ISOFIX. Rear-facing. Slidetech. Stroller Compatible. </em>With all the different rules and regulations, advice and new terminology, the world of car seats can leave you feeling confused and overwhelmed.</p><p></p><p>At Natural Baby Shower, we know the stakes are high when it comes to your little one’s safety. That’s why we’ve created this ultimate car seat buying guide, so you shopping for your newborn’s car seat can be as easy as clipping them in to their ISOFIX base.</p></div
          ></div
        ></div
      ></div
    ><div conditionals="" class="iQCaCkgSQpP4yhk60" data-instant-type="container" id="iQCaCkgSQpP4yhk60"
      ><div class="isLjLB08FNxVOz5IF current-car-seat-laws" data-instant-type="container"
        ><div class="idXB2OAi71Y2Cvjt7" data-instant-type="container"
          ><div data-instant-type="text" class="instant-rich-text iEFzaEibZritxEuqA"><h1>What are the current car seat laws?</h1></div
          ><div data-instant-type="text" class="instant-rich-text iSRJyVYYMWSh3p0oJ-WbtXIbGLwXv1oB6D"><p>You might have noticed a few car seat terms popping up that sound helpful—but perhaps you&apos;re not quite sure exactly what they mean. Let’s quickly cover some key features that can make life easier (and safer!) when you’re out and about with your baby.</p></div></div
        ><div class="iWoxqN9grJ1kdD9of-TOOKQpds9COvXxyg" data-instant-type="container"
          ><div data-instant-type="icon" class="iPewflgbpy8gIX5Hw-TOOKQpds9COvXxyg">
            <svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" fill="currentColor" viewBox="0 0 256 256" class="instant-icon">
              <title>check-circle</title><path d="M173.66,98.34a8,8,0,0,1,0,11.32l-56,56a8,8,0,0,1-11.32,0l-24-24a8,8,0,0,1,11.32-11.32L112,148.69l50.34-50.35A8,8,0,0,1,173.66,98.34ZM232,128A104,104,0,1,1,128,24,104.11,104.11,0,0,1,232,128Zm-16,0a88,88,0,1,0-88,88A88.1,88.1,0,0,0,216,128Z"></path>
            </svg></div
          ><div data-instant-type="text" class="instant-rich-text i4go7HVGbuoH3Ftk3-TOOKQpds9COvXxyg"><h3>Children must use a car seat from birth until 12 years old</h3></div
          ><div data-instant-type="text" class="instant-rich-text iLFV2zfW9FerEWhRu-TOOKQpds9COvXxyg"
            ><p><em>or 135cm tall, whichever comes first</em></p></div
          ></div
        ><div class="iWoxqN9grJ1kdD9of-AAqUVv3PS4boDo6M" data-instant-type="container"
          ><div data-instant-type="icon" class="iPewflgbpy8gIX5Hw-AAqUVv3PS4boDo6M">
            <svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" fill="currentColor" viewBox="0 0 256 256" class="instant-icon">
              <title>check-circle</title><path d="M173.66,98.34a8,8,0,0,1,0,11.32l-56,56a8,8,0,0,1-11.32,0l-24-24a8,8,0,0,1,11.32-11.32L112,148.69l50.34-50.35A8,8,0,0,1,173.66,98.34ZM232,128A104,104,0,1,1,128,24,104.11,104.11,0,0,1,232,128Zm-16,0a88,88,0,1,0-88,88A88.1,88.1,0,0,0,216,128Z"></path>
            </svg></div
          ><div data-instant-type="text" class="instant-rich-text i4go7HVGbuoH3Ftk3-AAqUVv3PS4boDo6M"><h3>Babies must be rear-facing until they are at least 15 months old</h3></div
          ><div data-instant-type="text" class="instant-rich-text iLFV2zfW9FerEWhRu-AAqUVv3PS4boDo6M"
            ><p><em>if using an i-Size seat</em></p></div
          ></div
        ><div class="iWoxqN9grJ1kdD9of-siBZw4x1JOQsdQwH" data-instant-type="container"
          ><div data-instant-type="icon" class="iPewflgbpy8gIX5Hw-siBZw4x1JOQsdQwH">
            <svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" fill="currentColor" viewBox="0 0 256 256" class="instant-icon">
              <title>check-circle</title><path d="M173.66,98.34a8,8,0,0,1,0,11.32l-56,56a8,8,0,0,1-11.32,0l-24-24a8,8,0,0,1,11.32-11.32L112,148.69l50.34-50.35A8,8,0,0,1,173.66,98.34ZM232,128A104,104,0,1,1,128,24,104.11,104.11,0,0,1,232,128Zm-16,0a88,88,0,1,0-88,88A88.1,88.1,0,0,0,216,128Z"></path>
            </svg></div
          ><div data-instant-type="text" class="instant-rich-text i4go7HVGbuoH3Ftk3-siBZw4x1JOQsdQwH"><h3>If you’re using a rear-facing seat in the front passenger seat, you must deactivate the airbag</h3></div
          ><div data-instant-type="text" class="instant-rich-text iLFV2zfW9FerEWhRu-siBZw4x1JOQsdQwH"><p>Most modern cars (made since around 2006) have built-in ISOFIX points. These are usually hidden between your car’s seat cushion and backrest. Your car manual will tell you exactly where these are, or you can physically feel for them. ISOFIX-compatible seats need these anchor points for installation.</p><p></p><p>If your car is older or doesn’t have ISOFIX, don’t panic! There are plenty of car seats designed for secure installation using just your car’s seat belt.</p></div></div
        ><div class="iWoxqN9grJ1kdD9of-4Rk9xFpi38rRGNAl" data-instant-type="container"
          ><div data-instant-type="icon" class="iPewflgbpy8gIX5Hw-4Rk9xFpi38rRGNAl">
            <svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" fill="currentColor" viewBox="0 0 256 256" class="instant-icon">
              <title>check-circle</title><path d="M173.66,98.34a8,8,0,0,1,0,11.32l-56,56a8,8,0,0,1-11.32,0l-24-24a8,8,0,0,1,11.32-11.32L112,148.69l50.34-50.35A8,8,0,0,1,173.66,98.34ZM232,128A104,104,0,1,1,128,24,104.11,104.11,0,0,1,232,128Zm-16,0a88,88,0,1,0-88,88A88.1,88.1,0,0,0,216,128Z"></path>
            </svg></div
          ><div data-instant-type="text" class="instant-rich-text i4go7HVGbuoH3Ftk3-4Rk9xFpi38rRGNAl"><h3>You can choose a child car seat based on your child’s height or weight.</h3></div
          ><div data-instant-type="text" class="instant-rich-text iLFV2zfW9FerEWhRu-4Rk9xFpi38rRGNAl"><p>Most modern cars (made since around 2006) have built-in ISOFIX points. These are usually hidden between your car’s seat cushion and backrest. Your car manual will tell you exactly where these are, or you can physically feel for them. ISOFIX-compatible seats need these anchor points for installation.</p><p></p><p>If your car is older or doesn’t have ISOFIX, don’t panic! There are plenty of car seats designed for secure installation using just your car’s seat belt.</p></div></div
        ></div
      ></div
    ><div class="iUEVuzBSMA4vOrNLZ" data-instant-type="container" id="iUEVuzBSMA4vOrNLZ"
      ><div class="iv9pCExnpINUHmlHG" data-instant-type="container"
        ><div data-instant-type="text" class="instant-rich-text i7pptc8CGFW4WkBp7"><h1>What type of car seat do you need?</h1></div
        ><div data-instant-type="text" class="instant-rich-text iSRJyVYYMWSh3p0oJ-A9d7O1Tx3m2lHv4Z"
          ><p>Thinking 12 years into the future might feel like a stretch when your little one hasn&apos;t even arrived yet—but <a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" class="instant-editor__link" href="https://www.naturalbabyshower.co.uk/blogs/b4baby/a-beginners-guide-to-choosing-the-right-car-seat-what-you-need-at-every-stage">choosing the right car seat</a> means keeping one eye on the years ahead. After all, your child will need a car seat until they&apos;re around 12 years old (or 135cm tall, whichever comes first).</p><p></p><p>There are several different types of car seats you’ll encounter as your child grows, each designed for different stages and lifestyles. Let&apos;s keep things clear and simple so you can confidently pick what’s right for your family at each stage.</p></div
        ></div
      ></div
