    ><div class="ixCg5qHT74uvvq9vq" data-instant-type="container" id="ixCg5qHT74uvvq9vq"
      ><div class="iNI58C49rXAdXRXmw" data-instant-type="container"
        ><div class="iAqFwBIwGXajm11Xn" data-instant-type="container"
          ><div data-instant-type="media" class="iDJxUIN3wpjER3EQJ"><img alt="" sizes="(max-width: 1280px) 100vw, 1280px" srcSet="https://cdn.instant.so/sites/XoayiDWI6O31eqEo/assets/UyrJXBP7cQNrF6UP/silver-cross-glide-plus-natural-taupe-flat-22.jpg?width=1080 1080w, https://cdn.instant.so/sites/XoayiDWI6O31eqEo/assets/UyrJXBP7cQNrF6UP/silver-cross-glide-plus-natural-taupe-flat-22.jpg?width=828 828w, https://cdn.instant.so/sites/XoayiDWI6O31eqEo/assets/UyrJXBP7cQNrF6UP/silver-cross-glide-plus-natural-taupe-flat-22.jpg?width=750 750w, https://cdn.instant.so/sites/XoayiDWI6O31eqEo/assets/UyrJXBP7cQNrF6UP/silver-cross-glide-plus-natural-taupe-flat-22.jpg?width=640 640w, https://cdn.instant.so/sites/XoayiDWI6O31eqEo/assets/UyrJXBP7cQNrF6UP/silver-cross-glide-plus-natural-taupe-flat-22.jpg?width=360 360w, https://cdn.instant.so/sites/XoayiDWI6O31eqEo/assets/UyrJXBP7cQNrF6UP/silver-cross-glide-plus-natural-taupe-flat-22.jpg?width=1280 1280w" src="https://cdn.instant.so/sites/XoayiDWI6O31eqEo/assets/UyrJXBP7cQNrF6UP/silver-cross-glide-plus-natural-taupe-flat-22.jpg?width=1280" width="1080" height="1080" decoding="async" loading="lazy" fetchpriority="auto" class="instant-media instant-image instant-image__main"></div></div
        ><div class="iom8b4TsL0hovDLhP" data-instant-type="container"
          ><div data-instant-type="text" class="instant-rich-text inxQdZtQlIjmRuhmL"><h1>Extra practical features worth considering</h1></div
          ><div class="ikXHlNAnGHmbcaUF0" data-instant-type="accordion-container" data-is-first-open="true" data-is-multi-open-enabled="false"
            ><div data-state="open" class="im618906UBeqzlO5Z" data-instant-type="accordion-item"
              ><button class="ipcydDjgDqIcPi7qS" data-instant-type="accordion-header" type="button"
                ><div data-instant-type="text" class="instant-rich-text ivjCgKppjYYWsQJA2"><h2>Harness holders or magnets</h2></div
                ><div data-instant-type="icon" class="i8e0gEyWQIwg4bIk4">
                  <svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" fill="currentColor" viewBox="0 0 256 256" class="instant-icon">
                    <title>caret-down</title><path d="M213.66,101.66l-80,80a8,8,0,0,1-11.32,0l-80-80A8,8,0,0,1,53.66,90.34L128,164.69l74.34-74.35a8,8,0,0,1,11.32,11.32Z"></path>
                  </svg></div></button
              ><div class="i0Z8e8bvKhAlpQ6Mz" data-instant-type="accordion-content" style="--instant-accordion-content-height:auto;--instant-accordion-content-width:auto"
                ><div data-instant-type="text" class="instant-rich-text inzeHVd2yasd1Hptf"><p>Harnesses can get tangled or trapped under your little one when you&apos;re getting them in and out—especially if you&apos;re in a hurry. Some seats include clever harness holders or magnets to hold the straps out of the way, meaning less fuss and frustration at the car door.</p></div></div
              ></div
            ><div data-state="closed" class="isFk0g4UMEPy7oCJH" data-instant-type="accordion-item"
              ><button class="i813R7tB3e8KJsI2c" data-instant-type="accordion-header" type="button"
                ><div data-instant-type="text" class="instant-rich-text i9R9tp7WUn6URL6xy"><h2>UPF50+ sun canopy</h2></div
                ><div data-instant-type="icon" class="ijSL6fieWSTyoqjbC">
                  <svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" fill="currentColor" viewBox="0 0 256 256" class="instant-icon">
                    <title>caret-down</title><path d="M213.66,101.66l-80,80a8,8,0,0,1-11.32,0l-80-80A8,8,0,0,1,53.66,90.34L128,164.69l74.34-74.35a8,8,0,0,1,11.32,11.32Z"></path>
                  </svg></div></button
              ><div class="ibJzrtTUYJeJ3kafr" data-instant-type="accordion-content" style="--instant-accordion-content-height:auto;--instant-accordion-content-width:auto"
                ><div data-instant-type="text" class="instant-rich-text i7zvczWHA42Dp67qt"><p>If you&apos;re often out and about, a built-in UPF50+ canopy on your car seat can be a lifesaver. Not only does it protect your little one from harmful UV rays, but it also keeps them comfortable and shaded, helping to avoid those mid-journey meltdowns on bright, sunny days.</p></div></div
              ></div
            ><div data-state="closed" class="ivQaQE8CXdqsknjua" data-instant-type="accordion-item"
              ><button class="iAoCaUJlU119B0e1K" data-instant-type="accordion-header" type="button"
                ><div data-instant-type="text" class="instant-rich-text ioks52njYCudzlwI9"><h2>Removable newborn inserts</h2></div
                ><div data-instant-type="icon" class="iHUWsxcwTjLw1VrPP">
                  <svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" fill="currentColor" viewBox="0 0 256 256" class="instant-icon">
                    <title>caret-down</title><path d="M213.66,101.66l-80,80a8,8,0,0,1-11.32,0l-80-80A8,8,0,0,1,53.66,90.34L128,164.69l74.34-74.35a8,8,0,0,1,11.32,11.32Z"></path>
                  </svg></div></button
              ><div class="iKjQ41UaLuI48gIbB" data-instant-type="accordion-content" style="--instant-accordion-content-height:auto;--instant-accordion-content-width:auto"
                ><div data-instant-type="text" class="instant-rich-text ieFpyA79Ukpbd7WUJ"><p>Many infant car seats come with special padded inserts to keep newborns snug and safe. These inserts should be easily removable as your little one grows. Look for inserts that adjust or detach to give your baby a comfy fit as they develop.</p></div></div
              ></div
            ><div data-state="closed" class="iz9bNps3chQJNTIzj" data-instant-type="accordion-item"
              ><button class="i31V1IKLPGhN73slY" data-instant-type="accordion-header" type="button"
                ><div data-instant-type="text" class="instant-rich-text iwepjNS2xpBADcktQ"><h2>Lightweight design</h2></div
                ><div data-instant-type="icon" class="i1QAQDcRl45UXzpIh">
                  <svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" fill="currentColor" viewBox="0 0 256 256" class="instant-icon">
                    <title>caret-down</title><path d="M213.66,101.66l-80,80a8,8,0,0,1-11.32,0l-80-80A8,8,0,0,1,53.66,90.34L128,164.69l74.34-74.35a8,8,0,0,1,11.32,11.32Z"></path>
                  </svg></div></button
              ><div class="iA3RqlmScT7Jez5ZZ" data-instant-type="accordion-content" style="--instant-accordion-content-height:auto;--instant-accordion-content-width:auto"
                ><div data-instant-type="text" class="instant-rich-text ipX2KaRZOwKVb5m6p"><p>If you&apos;re frequently lifting your infant seat in and out of the car or carrying it on errands, weight matters. Some car seats are specifically designed to be lightweight without sacrificing safety or quality, making them more practical for everyday use.</p></div></div
              ></div
            ><div data-state="closed" class="imY9vgiRDb5q2eSMk" data-instant-type="accordion-item"
              ><button class="i4BKESMXRjr4UgE5B" data-instant-type="accordion-header" type="button"
                ><div data-instant-type="text" class="instant-rich-text ig3dFnJEyK4t38gMS"><h2>Adjustable recline positions</h2></div
                ><div data-instant-type="icon" class="iMGhEz4oopwl52wZC">
                  <svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" fill="currentColor" viewBox="0 0 256 256" class="instant-icon">
                    <title>caret-down</title><path d="M213.66,101.66l-80,80a8,8,0,0,1-11.32,0l-80-80A8,8,0,0,1,53.66,90.34L128,164.69l74.34-74.35a8,8,0,0,1,11.32,11.32Z"></path>
                  </svg></div></button
              ><div class="ivmRsCL08QEdimwAn" data-instant-type="accordion-content" style="--instant-accordion-content-height:auto;--instant-accordion-content-width:auto"
                ><div data-instant-type="text" class="instant-rich-text iuKZvtGvidRVY7OE7"><p>Seats that offer multiple recline positions give you more flexibility to keep your baby comfortable, whether they&apos;re napping or awake. Adjustable recline also helps with safe positioning, especially for younger babies who can’t yet hold their heads up securely.</p></div></div
              ></div
            ></div
          ></div
        ></div
      ></div
    ><div class="i4ELJA0oJOCTvZFfg" data-instant-type="container" id="i4ELJA0oJOCTvZFfg"
      ><div class="iBxj2IF7xtqLFCWHA" data-instant-type="container"
        ><div class="i3fQCnhTeJk5gXH5z" data-instant-type="container"
          ><div class="iO8qkaUvwf83xqTs1" data-instant-type="container"
            ><div class="isnukV9CUwIwcXVg5" data-instant-type="container"
              ><div data-instant-type="text" class="instant-rich-text ikhqfnLWGAthdALhX"><h1>Rear-facing car seats: Why you should rear-face as long as possible</h1></div
              ><div data-instant-type="text" class="instant-rich-text ilrdVhZlujDR4kIwO"><p>In a head-on collision, a rear-facing car seat supports your child’s head, neck, and spine much better than a forward-facing seat. Babies and toddlers have delicate bones, muscles, and ligaments that aren’t fully developed yet. When they&apos;re rear-facing, the force of a collision spreads evenly across their entire body, dramatically reducing the risk of serious injury.</p><p></p><p>In fact, studies show that children are five times safer when rear-facing. This simple positioning choice can literally be lifesaving.</p></div></div
            ><div class="i8VbK7To4CIWM0QBr" data-instant-type="container"
              ><div class="iwnUjBckYz7YltAkW" data-instant-type="container"
                ><div class="itKdZxfMhXIuoKKV5" data-instant-type="container"
                  ><div data-instant-type="text" class="instant-rich-text ioqmQ7I7SHCz7dVRC"><h3>15</h3></div
                  ><div data-instant-type="text" class="instant-rich-text iOtXHIjDihxCJ3VQQ"><p>months - the minimum age to forward face</p></div></div
                ><div class="it8qiXMp6OOvTzNnK" data-instant-type="container"
                  ><div data-instant-type="text" class="instant-rich-text iyFLQHAjE4KYnq30Y"><h3>5</h3></div
                  ><div data-instant-type="text" class="instant-rich-text it3lJVhifeWzcrC6L"><p>times safer to rear face than forward face</p></div></div
                ></div
              ></div
            ><a class="iBmdS7Wev3UuGZqaH-19urTY0OF8l8lfmD" data-instant-type="container" href="https://www.naturalbabyshower.co.uk/blogs/b4baby/the-benefits-of-extended-rear-facing-car-seats-with-besafe?_pos=408&amp;_sid=60774070f&amp;_ss=r" rel="noopener noreferrer"
              ><div data-instant-type="text" class="instant-rich-text iVP0AB4lMetc42Gxw-19urTY0OF8l8lfmD"><p>Learn more</p></div></a
